## Scope: what is and is not covered

This repository contains three kinds of material, and the license applies to all of it — but the practical effect differs.

| Part | Contents | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| **The manuscript** | `Book/` — chapters, appendices, glossary, answer keys | The prose this license primarily exists to cover. |
| **The labs** | `Labs/` — lab instructions, notes scaffolds, worksheets, answer keys | Reusable in teaching under the license terms. See below on internal training. |
| **The simulated data and generators** | `Data/` — CSV and text datasets, and the `generate.py` scripts that produce them | Licensed the same way. If you need the generator scripts under permissive terms for a tool you are building, open an issue and ask — a dual-license for `Data/**/generate.py` is a reasonable request. |

### The cover image

`Book/figures/cover.png` is **not** covered by this license unless the copyright holder says otherwise. Cover art is frequently produced under separate terms — commissioned, stock-licensed, or generated under a service agreement with its own conditions. Confirm the terms attached to the cover before redistributing it, and do not assume the CC license extends to it.

### Third-party material

Tool names, trademarks, and logos referenced in the text belong to their respective owners. Links to external tools, datasets, and documentation carry whatever license those projects apply — notably [Hayabusa](https://github.com/Yamato-Security/hayabusa) (AGPL-3.0), [Volatility 3](https://www.volatilityfoundation.org/) (Volatility Software License), [MemProcFS](https://github.com/ufrisk/MemProcFS) (GPL-3.0), and the [EVTX-to-MITRE-Attack](https://github.com/mdecrevoisier/EVTX-to-MITRE-Attack) dataset (CC0). Nothing here relicenses any of them.

